---
layout: base.njk
title: Mods — Thurbox
description: Official and community mods for Thurbox, discovered from the thurbox-mods GitHub topic.
extraCss: [mods.css]
activeNav: mods
footer: true
navScrolled: true
---
<div class="container plugin-page">
  <header class="plugin-intro">
    <p class="plugin-eyebrow">Extend your workspace</p>
    <h1>Mods</h1>
    <p>Panes, extensions and themes published on GitHub, discovered automatically from the <a href="https://github.com/topics/thurbox-mods"><code>thurbox-mods</code></a> topic. Install one with its command, then follow its README for setup.</p>
    <p><a href="#submit-mod">Publish yours</a> · <a href="./docs/interface.html">Mod guide</a></p>
  </header>
  <p class="plugin-notice">Official mods are maintained by Thurbeen. Community mods list themselves with the topic and are not reviewed by Thurbeen: read the README and check the capability grants a mod asks for before you install it.</p>
  <form class="plugin-filters" id="plugin-filters" hidden role="search" aria-label="Search and sort mods">
    <div><label for="plugin-search">Search mods</label><input id="plugin-search" type="search" placeholder="Name, owner, topic or description" /></div>
    <div><label for="plugin-sort">Sort by</label><select id="plugin-sort"><option value="popular">Popular</option><option value="updated">Recently updated</option><option value="newest">Newest</option><option value="name">Name</option></select></div>
    <div><label for="plugin-badge">Maintainer</label><select id="plugin-badge"><option value="">All maintainers</option><option value="official">Official</option><option value="community">Community</option></select></div>
    <button type="reset">Reset</button>
  </form>
  <p id="plugin-count" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">{{ gallery | length }} mods</p>
  <noscript><p>All mods are listed below, most starred first. Enable JavaScript to search, filter and sort.</p></noscript>
  <div class="plugin-grid" id="plugin-grid">
    {% for mod in gallery %}
    {% set badge = "official" if mod.official else "community" %}
    <article class="plugin-card" data-plugin data-badge="{{ badge }}" data-stars="{{ mod.stars }}" data-pushed="{{ mod.pushedAt | escape }}" data-created="{{ mod.createdAt | escape }}" data-name="{{ mod.name | lower | escape }}">
      <div class="plugin-card-head">
        <img class="plugin-avatar" src="https://github.com/{{ mod.owner | urlencode }}.png?size=64" alt="" width="32" height="32" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="plugin-title">
          <h2><a href="{{ mod.repo | escape }}">{{ mod.name | escape }}</a></h2>
          <p class="plugin-owner">by <a href="https://github.com/{{ mod.owner | urlencode }}">{{ mod.owner | escape }}</a></p>
        </div>
        <span class="plugin-badge plugin-badge--{{ badge }}">{{ badge | capitalize }}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="plugin-desc">{{ mod.description | escape }}</p>
      {% if mod.media %}
      <a class="plugin-preview" href="{{ mod.repo | escape }}#readme"><img src="{{ mod.media.url | escape }}" alt="{{ mod.media.alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
      {% else %}
      <div class="plugin-preview"><div class="plugin-preview-placeholder"><span aria-hidden="true">&gt;_</span>No preview yet<br /><a href="{{ mod.repo | escape }}#readme">Explore the README</a></div></div>
      {% endif %}
      <dl class="plugin-meta">
        <div><dt>Stars</dt><dd class="plugin-stars">{{ mod.stars }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Last update</dt><dd><time datetime="{{ mod.pushedAt | escape }}">{{ mod.pushedAt.slice(0, 10) | escape }}</time></dd></div>
        {% if mod.version %}<div><dt>Version</dt><dd>{{ mod.version | escape }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {% if mod.requiresThurbox %}<div><dt>Thurbox</dt><dd>{{ mod.requiresThurbox | escape }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {% if mod.platforms | length %}<div><dt>Platforms</dt><dd>{{ mod.platforms | join(', ') | escape }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
      </dl>
      {% if mod.topics | length %}
      <ul class="plugin-topics" aria-label="Topics">
        {% for topic in mod.topics %}<li><a href="https://github.com/topics/{{ topic | urlencode }}">{{ topic | escape }}</a></li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% endif %}
      <details class="plugin-install"><summary>Install command</summary><pre data-wrap data-title="Install"><code class="language-bash">{{ mod.install | escape }}</code></pre></details>
      {% if mod.notes %}<p class="plugin-notes">{{ mod.notes | escape }}</p>{% endif %}
      <a href="{{ mod.repo | escape }}#readme">Repository &amp; setup →</a>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p id="plugin-empty" hidden>No mods match these filters. Try another search or reset the filters.</p>
  <section class="plugin-submit" id="submit-mod" aria-labelledby="submit-heading">
    <h2 id="submit-heading">Publish your mod</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Publish the mod in a public GitHub repository.</li>
      <li>Add the <a href="https://github.com/topics/thurbox-mods"><code>thurbox-mods</code></a> topic to the repository.</li>
      <li>Optional: put a screenshot or GIF at <code>media/demo.gif</code>, or describe the listing in your <code>mod.toml</code>, as below.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The site rebuilds every day. It reads each repository’s name, owner, description, stars, last push and topics from GitHub, and its version and required Thurbox version from <code>mod.toml</code>. Forks and archived repositories are left out. No pull request and no review queue.</p>
    <pre data-title="mod.toml"><code class="language-toml">[gallery]
media = "media/demo.gif"
media_alt = "What the screenshot shows"
platforms = ["Linux", "macOS"]
notes = "Required capability grants, layout changes and conflicts."</code></pre>
    <p>Every field is optional. <code>media</code> is a path in the repository or an HTTPS URL. The install command is <code>thurbox-cli mod install git+</code> and the repository URL. A mod that needs another command asks for it in the reviewed overlay. The <a href="https://github.com/Thurbeen/thurbox/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#mod-gallery">contributing guide</a> describes the curated overlay that maintainers use for notes and removals.</p>
    <details><summary>Official repositories outside this gallery</summary><p><a href="https://github.com/Thurbeen/thurbox-plugin-orchestrator">thurbox-plugin-orchestrator</a> is archived and targets the earlier admin plugin model. <a href="https://github.com/Thurbeen/thurbox-discord">thurbox-discord</a> manages the community Discord server; it is not a Thurbox add-on.</p></details>
  </section>
</div>
<script src="./js/mods.js"></script>
